comments:
I changed [L1210](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/main/subsys/mgmt/hawkbit/hawkbit.c#L1210) from
```c
	if (boot_request_upgrade(BOOT_UPGRADE_TEST)) {
		LOG_ERR("Download failed");
		hb_context.code_status = HAWKBIT_DOWNLOAD_ERROR;
	} else {
		hb_context.code_status = HAWKBIT_UPDATE_INSTALLED;
		hawkbit_device_acid_update(hb_context.json_action_id);
	}
```

to

```c
	if ((boot_request_upgrade(BOOT_UPGRADE_TEST)) ||
	  (k_sem_take(&hb_context.semaphore, K_NO_WAIT) != 0)) {
		LOG_ERR("Download failed");
		hb_context.code_status = HAWKBIT_DOWNLOAD_ERROR;
	} else {
		hb_context.code_status = HAWKBIT_UPDATE_INSTALLED;
		hawkbit_device_acid_update(hb_context.json_action_id);
	}
```

and now the `hawkbit_probe` is able to detect that the download failed and will initiate a new download during the next probe.

## EDIT:

I don't think we need a semaphore for this purpose, a boolean should be enough
